  "body": "### Fixed\r\n- `CommandMifareClassicAuthenticate` now also recognizes the `6982` status word (\"Security status not satisfied\", returned by the Keyple storage card APDU interpreter as specified by the Keyple Plugin Storage Card API) as an authentication failure, in addition to `6300` (returned by PC/SC readers). An authentication failure through the interpreter now raises `SCAuthenticationFailedException` instead of `SCInvalidCardResponseException`.\r\n### Tests\r\n- Added a unit test covering the `6982` authentication failure status word.\r\n### Upgraded\r\n- `keyple-util-java-lib` from `2.4.1` to `2.5.0`\r\n"
}
